IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-application`
IMPORT `cp6-provinces-and-consent`

-- Tests of cp6-provinces-and-consent.l4 (sections 113 and 114, and subsection 113.1(12)).
-- The sums are worked by hand in the comments.

§ `Tests -- a province leaves the plan; changes that need consent`

§§ `Section 113(1)(a): the obligation ceases from the day the regulation becomes effective`

-- Notice on 15 June 2026: effective on the first day of the third year following the year of the notice, 1 January 2029 (section 3(3)).
-- Inputs: a regulation has been made; the obligation is of the kind; it concerns contributions in that province; the date of the notice; the day.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2029 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2035 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2028 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2030 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2030 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1)(a) — the obligation or liability ceases to be one with respect to the payment of benefits under this Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2030 1 1))

§§ `Section 113(1)(b): the securities and the balance`

-- Amount 1,144,000. The province's securities are used first, then Canada's, then the balance is paid.
-- Province 800,000 and Canada 500,000: 800,000 from the province; 344,000 from Canada; no balance.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` 1144000 800000 EQUALS 800000
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of Canada's designated securities transferred in the second instance` 1144000 800000 500000 EQUALS 344000
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the balance paid to the government of the province in a prescribed manner` 1144000 800000 500000 EQUALS 0
-- Province 300,000 and Canada 400,000: 300,000; then 400,000 (all Canada can give); balance 1,144,000 less 700,000 is 444,000.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` 1144000 300000 EQUALS 300000
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of Canada's designated securities transferred in the second instance` 1144000 300000 400000 EQUALS 400000
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the balance paid to the government of the province in a prescribed manner` 1144000 300000 400000 EQUALS 444000
-- The province's securities cover the whole amount: nothing from Canada, no balance.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` 1144000 2000000 EQUALS 1144000
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of Canada's designated securities transferred in the second instance` 1144000 2000000 500000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the balance paid to the government of the province in a prescribed manner` 1144000 2000000 500000 EQUALS 0
-- No securities at all: the whole amount is the balance.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the balance paid to the government of the province in a prescribed manner` 1144000 0 0 EQUALS 1144000
-- A nil amount moves nothing.
#ASSERT `s 113(1)(b) — the value of the province's designated securities transferred in the first instance` 0 800000 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `s 113(1.1) — the Minister of Finance may by notice require the Investment Board to pay the amount and transfer the securities` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1.1) — the Minister of Finance may by notice require the Investment Board to pay the amount and transfer the securities` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(1.1) — the Minister of Finance may by notice require the Investment Board to pay the amount and transfer the securities` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Section 113(2): the amount to be paid`

-- (a) 1,000,000 plus (b) 250,000 less (c) 100,000 less (d): 60,000 of costs times 1,000,000 over 10,000,000 of all contributions = 6,000. 1,150,000 less 100,000 less 6,000 = 1,144,000... worked: 1,000,000 + 250,000 = 1,250,000; less 100,000 = 1,150,000; less 6,000 = 1,144,000.
#ASSERT `s 113(2) — the amount to be paid to the government of the province` 1000000 250000 100000 60000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 1144000
-- No costs of administration: 1,250,000 less 100,000.
#ASSERT `s 113(2) — the amount to be paid to the government of the province` 1000000 250000 100000 0 10000000 EQUALS JUST 1150000
-- The province supplied all the contributions: (d) is all the costs, 500. 4,000,000 less 500.
#ASSERT `s 113(2) — the amount to be paid to the government of the province` 4000000 0 0 500 4000000 EQUALS JUST 3999500
-- Not covered: no contributions at all, so no proportion.
#ASSERT `s 113(2) — the amount to be paid to the government of the province` 0 0 0 500 0 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 113(3) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(3) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113(3) — the Minister may enter into an agreement with the government of the province` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Section 114(1): included provinces`

`cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province B"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

`cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province A"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS TRUE

`cp6 test Yukon` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Yukon"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

`cp6 test Northwest Territories` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "the Northwest Territories"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

`cp6 test Nunavut` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Nunavut"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

-- Inputs: the province; an agreement under subsection 4(3) is in force at the time.
#ASSERT `s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test province providing a comprehensive pension plan` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test Yukon` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test Northwest Territories` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test Nunavut` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(1) — a province is an included province` `cp6 test Yukon` TRUE)

§§ `Section 114(2): the earliest day a major amendment may come into force`

-- A notice laid in 2026: the years following are 2027, 2028 and 2029, so the first day of the third is 1 January 2029.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2029 1 1
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` 2030 EQUALS YMD 2033 1 1
-- The core reads section 3(3), "the first day of the third year following the year in which the notice ... was given", the same way.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the earliest day on which the provision may come into force` 2026 EQUALS `s 3(3) — the day a regulation under subsection (2) becomes effective` (YMD 2026 6 15)

-- Inputs: the way the change comes about; alters the general level of benefits; alters a contribution rate.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `an enactment of Parliament` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `an enactment of Parliament` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `an enactment of Parliament` FALSE FALSE)
-- A regulation or a deemed amendment is not an enactment of Parliament and is taken out by 113.1(12) and 114(4.1).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(2) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(2)` `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)` TRUE TRUE)

-- Inputs: the way; alters benefits; alters a rate; the year of the notice; the day is fixed by order of the Governor in Council; the day.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` TRUE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YMD 2029 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` TRUE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YMD 2031 7 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` TRUE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YMD 2028 12 31) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` TRUE FALSE 2026 FALSE (YMD 2030 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: a provision that alters neither benefits nor rates is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) — the provision may come into force on a day` `an enactment of Parliament` FALSE FALSE 2026 TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 114(3): the notice of intention`

#ASSERT `s 114(3) — the notice of intention is in the form the subsection requires` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(3) — the notice of intention is in the form the subsection requires` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 114(3) — the Minister must forthwith cause a copy of the notice to be sent to the lieutenant governor in council of each included province` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(3) — the Minister must forthwith cause a copy of the notice to be sent to the lieutenant governor in council of each included province` FALSE)

§§ `Section 114(4): other amendments of substance need the provinces' consent`

#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the classes of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the contribution rate, first additional contribution rate or second additional contribution rate for employees, employers or self-employed persons for any year` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the formulae for calculating the contributions and benefits payable under the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the management or operation of the Canada Pension Plan Account or the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `an enactment of Parliament` `some other matter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Subsection (4.1) takes the deemed changes out of (4).
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered (fork C6-F17): whether (4) reaches a regulation under 113.1(6).
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the provision is subject to subsection 114(4)` `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The two-thirds test. Nine included provinces: six is two thirds exactly, five is not. Population 30,000,000: 20,000,000 is two thirds exactly.
-- Inputs: the number of included provinces; the number that consented; the population of all of them; the population of those that consented.
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 9 6 30000000 20000000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 9 5 30000000 29000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 9 9 30000000 19999999)
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 9 9 30000000 20000001
-- Ten provinces: seven is more than two thirds (6.67), six is not.
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 10 7 30000000 25000000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 10 6 30000000 25000000)
-- Three provinces: two is two thirds exactly.
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 3 2 3000 2000
-- Both limbs are needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4) — the consent of at least two thirds of the included provinces, having at least two thirds of their population, has been signified` 9 6 30000000 10000000)

-- Inputs: the way; the matter; consent has been signified.
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` `an enactment of Parliament` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` `an enactment of Parliament` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` `an enactment of Parliament` `some other matter` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 114(4) — the order fixing the day for the provision may be made and has force` `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2` `the general level of benefits provided by the Act` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 114(4.1) and subsection 113.1(12): the changes taken out`

#ASSERT `s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)`
#ASSERT `s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)`
#ASSERT `s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` `an enactment of Parliament`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 114(4.1) — subsections 114(2) and (4) do not apply to the change` `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2`)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` `a regulation under subsection 113.1(6) amending Schedule 1 or 2`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 1 under subsections 113.1(11.05) to (11.11)`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` `a deemed amendment of Schedule 2 under subsection 113.1(11.141)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` `a determination of the portions of benefits under subsection 113.1(11.142)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(12) — subsection 114(2) does not apply to the amendment of Schedule 1 or 2` `an enactment of Parliament`)

§§ `Section 114(5): the day population is taken`

#ASSERT `s 114(5) — the day on which the population of a province is taken for a year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
